Skip the "invalidate the old area first" step of a style change for a widget
that has never been rendered. LVGL 9.6 runs it while a new widget applies its
theme, so every widget created invalidates a 1x1 area at the screen origin,
and creating a hidden overlay redraws and flushes an unchanged frame. A widget
that has never been drawn has no old pixels to clear.

diff --git a/src/core/lv_obj_style.c b/src/core/lv_obj_style.c
--- a/src/core/lv_obj_style.c
+++ b/src/core/lv_obj_style.c
@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@
